From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] opkg-make-index: never rescan the morgue or locales
 directories

os.walk() descends into the morgue/ directory that -m itself creates
(and into the -L locales tree).  Every morgued package is re-read on
every run, and worse: a morgue copy whose version compares >= the live
copy displaces it in the index (add_package returns 0 for equal
versions), publishing "Filename: morgue/foo.ipk" and moving the live
file into the morgue.  Re-morguing a morgue file also fails with a
nested morgue/morgue rename.  Prune both directories from the walk.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
--- a/opkg-make-index
+++ b/opkg-make-index
@@ -102,7 +102,16 @@
 
     files = []
     opkg_extensions = ['.ipk', '.opk', '.deb']
-    for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(pkg_dir):
+    for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(pkg_dir):
+        # Never descend into the morgue or the locales tree: packages there
+        # have already been superseded or moved aside.  If a morgue copy
+        # re-enters the scan it can displace the live package (equal versions
+        # compare >= 0 in add_package) and publish a Filename: pointing into
+        # morgue/, and re-morguing it fails with a nested morgue/morgue path.
+        skip_dirs = ['morgue']
+        if locales_dir:
+            skip_dirs.append(os.path.basename(locales_dir))
+        dirnames[:] = [d for d in dirnames if d not in skip_dirs]
         for filename in filenames:
             ext = os.path.splitext(filename)[1]
             if ext in opkg_extensions:
